{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim","id":1561637,"title":"Why No Accurate Nephilim?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-12T13:33:03-07:00","id":1561637,"title":"Why No Accurate Nephilim?","content":"Okay, so over my decades of playing games, reading stories, and watching TV / Movies, I've seen the term <i>&quot;Nephilim&quot;</i> tossed around for quite a lot of characters. But never have I seen them be presented as anywhere even remotely accurate to the very creatures for which they are supposedly named.<br /> <br /> <br /> At best, they'll depict a Nephilim as being half angel, but that's as far as accuracy goes, before they veer off in a completely different direction. While yes, the Nephilim were the offspring of angels mating with humans, it was much worse than that.<br /> <br /> The Nephilim were a race of giants, who inherited the powers of angels and used them to tyrannically oppress the humans living on their land. They also had insatiable appetites which drove them to exhaust all available food sources in the land, before eventually turning to cannibalism in order to stave off their hunger.<br /> <br /> When God found out about their existence, he was so outraged, that he ordered their complete extermination.<br /> <br /> <br /> So why is it that so many fictional media, Curseborne included fail to get this bit of mythology correct? Even if the original Nephilim were wiped out, that's not to say that a new generation couldn't be created.<br /> <br /> Heck, that story could actually serve as a basis for WHY they became a family of outcasts in the first place. It's because their creation is now considered to be taboo, and the Outsiders don't want anything to do with them, lest they piss off a higher power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T13:34:51-07:00","id":1561638,"title":"","content":"<b>Slight Correction:</b> the Dominions series actually does present the Nephilim as the cannibalistic giants they're meant to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T13:40:46-07:00","id":1561639,"title":"","content":"For the same reason we don't see accurate angels: because for most stories it wouldn't be interesting, even if the very few that would, would be quite so.<br /> <br /> You can do a lot more with a humanlike character capable of normal interaction with the others than with an eldritch abomination of an insatiable half-Cthulhu giant.<br /> <br /> Add to that how legends and pop-culture spreads, the fact it wouldn't be intuitive for most people, but mainly because most authors find humanoid characters easier to write about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T15:20:43-07:00","id":1561642,"title":"","content":"The idea of accurate Nephilim is nonsensical. Accurate to what? The Bible?<br /> <br /> Genesis 6:4 &quot;The Nephilim were in the earth in those days, and also after that, when the Bene Elohim came in unto the daughters of men, and they bore children to them; the same were the mighty men that were of old, the men of renown.&quot;<br /> <br /> I didn't translate Bene Elohim because how you translate it stems from a lot of theological assumptions. But most importantly this is not a phrase that originally meant &quot;angels&quot; as those are divine messengers. The oldest meaning of Bene Elohim would be the deities of the Canaanite pantheon (as the Canaanites treated them as all the sons - Bene - of the high deity El), and pre-hard monotheist Israelite traditions would have also interpreted this similarly. It's only after the Babylonian Exile that Jewish theology shifted towards monotheism and the Israelite deity merged with El, and thus all of the early traditions of the Bene Elohim had to be reconstructed as servants of this new single deity.<br /> <br /> The phrasing itself is unclear if the Nephilim are their own thing, the Bene Elohim that mated with human women, or the offspring who we're supposed to then associate with demigods and mythological heroes from ancient epics (the mighty men and men of renown).<br /> <br /> Numbers 13:33 &quot;And there we saw the Nephilim, the sons of Anak, who come of the Nephilim; and we were in our own sight as grasshoppers, and so we were in their sight.&quot;<br /> <br /> The context of this is that it's the end of the report by the spies sent to scout the land of Canaan before the Israelites end the Exodus and claim the land for themselves. This is where the idea of them being giants probably comes from. Though they're never called giants (and we have characters like Goliath later that repeat the theme of there just being some really big guys among the tribes already living there).<br /> <br /> And that's it. That's all the information you're going to get out of the Bible and older traditions. You have to jump centuries until you get to Enoch 1 and other late post-Exilic writings where we see interpretations of the Nephilim that actually give us any details. And those texts are not uniform in where the Nephilim came from, if they were even inherently bad, and what traits they had that separated them from normal humans.<br /> <br /> Claiming anyone &quot;gets them wrong,&quot; is a far greater negative comment on yourself than it is on any author using them for fiction characters/creatures. If you think there's some authoritative source for an accurate depiction of the Nephilim, you need to do a lot more reading on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T09:34:47-07:00","id":1561769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561642#post1561642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of accurate Nephilim is nonsensical. Accurate to what? The Bible?<br /> <br /> Genesis 6:4 &quot;The Nephilim were in the earth in those days, and also after that, when the Bene Elohim came in unto the daughters of men, and they bore children to them; the same were the mighty men that were of old, the men of renown.&quot;<br /> <br /> I didn't translate Bene Elohim because how you translate it stems from a lot of theological assumptions. But most importantly this is not a phrase that originally meant &quot;angels&quot; as those are divine messengers. The oldest meaning of Bene Elohim would be the deities of the Canaanite pantheon (as the Canaanites treated them as all the sons - Bene - of the high deity El), and pre-hard monotheist Israelite traditions would have also interpreted this similarly. It's only after the Babylonian Exile that Jewish theology shifted towards monotheism and the Israelite deity merged with El, and thus all of the early traditions of the Bene Elohim had to be reconstructed as servants of this new single deity.<br /> <br /> The phrasing itself is unclear if the Nephilim are their own thing, the Bene Elohim that mated with human women, or the offspring who we're supposed to then associate with demigods and mythological heroes from ancient epics (the mighty men and men of renown).<br /> <br /> Numbers 13:33 &quot;And there we saw the Nephilim, the sons of Anak, who come of the Nephilim; and we were in our own sight as grasshoppers, and so we were in their sight.&quot;<br /> <br /> The context of this is that it's the end of the report by the spies sent to scout the land of Canaan before the Israelites end the Exodus and claim the land for themselves. This is where the idea of them being giants probably comes from. Though they're never called giants (and we have characters like Goliath later that repeat the theme of there just being some really big guys among the tribes already living there).<br /> <br /> And that's it. That's all the information you're going to get out of the Bible and older traditions. You have to jump centuries until you get to Enoch 1 and other late post-Exilic writings where we see interpretations of the Nephilim that actually give us any details. And those texts are not uniform in where the Nephilim came from, if they were even inherently bad, and what traits they had that separated them from normal humans.<br /> <br /> Claiming anyone &quot;gets them wrong,&quot; is a far greater negative comment on yourself than it is on any author using them for fiction characters/creatures. If you think there's some authoritative source for an accurate depiction of the Nephilim, you need to do a lot more reading on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your take on this Heavy Arms, I find it very NOT one sided, which is more than I can say for the OP in this case. No offence meant to you Dark King but I find the take you presented to be one sided and overly loyal to the bible, which is, in my opinion, a heavily biased source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T10:00:06-07:00","id":1561770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561769#post1561769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your take on this Heavy Arms, I find it very NOT one sided, which is more than I can say for the OP in this case. No offence meant to you Dark King but I find the take you presented to be one sided and overly loyal to the bible, which is, in my opinion, a heavily biased source.</div> </div> </div> </div>How exactly is it biased to ask that a creature from real world mythology be depicted in a way that remains faithful to it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry, forgot this was Curseborne, not Scion. Removed the rest of my reply!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":".  Wrong Gameline. 07-16-2026, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T10:11:10-07:00","id":1561772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561770#post1561770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly is it biased to ask that a creature from real world mythology be depicted in a way that remains faithful to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The bias is in assuming a specific depiction is the true myth without researching the subject, as Heavy Arms demonstrated.<br /> <br /> Neither is the bible consistent about how they are, or even what they are, nor is it the only real source of mythology about them.<br /> <br /> You would know that had you researched the matter. You didn't, you assumed your cultural depiction was objectively right. That's bias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T10:16:32-07:00","id":1561773,"title":"","content":"DarkKing: You're not asking people to be faithful to real world mythology, you're asking people to be faithful to ancient fanfiction that was rejected by Jewish and early Christian theologians as such.<br /> <br /> Nobody alive today knows how to accurate depict the Nephilim because nobody knows enough about them to do so. Either you have to skip them completely, or treat them as a blank slate just like ancient Exilic Jewish authors did. If you pick the writings of said Exilic writers you're still picking and choosing which you're listening to, and you're inevitably ignoring older source texts on some level.<br /> <br /> As I think I've said enough times, you're talking about <b>my</b> culture's myths. I've written long posts about how wrong people get the Golem myths. I get the desire to have more respectful treatments of real myths, but there's limits. &quot;Nobody knows what accurate would be,&quot; is a limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T11:10:34-07:00","id":1561776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561773#post1561773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I think I've said enough times, you're talking about <b>my</b> culture's myths. I've written long posts about how wrong people get the Golem myths. I get the desire to have more respectful treatments of real myths, but there's limits. &quot;Nobody knows what accurate would be,&quot; is a limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to clarify?<br /> <br /> Closest I have to a real life knowledge about golems comes from <i>'The Golem and the Rabi'</i>, which I haven't read since I think elementary school.<br /> <br /> Are they not supposed to be guardians of some kind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T13:45:17-07:00","id":1561780,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1452173-cultural-appropriation-in-gaming?p=1452689#post1452689\">As I said, I've written about it already.</a><br /> <br /> That said, getting into golems isn't really the point of why I mentioned it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T14:42:04-07:00","id":1561784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561780#post1561780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, getting into golems isn't really the point of why I mentioned it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still a fascinating subject, but thanks for the link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-28T11:40:44-07:00","id":1564390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561642#post1561642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Numbers 13:33 &quot;And there we saw the Nephilim, the sons of Anak, who come of the Nephilim; and we were in our own sight as grasshoppers, and so we were in their sight.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly reinforcing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> here, but this part was said by spies who were immediately accused of, and punished for, lying about it. So even if you take the Bible seriously, this passage doesn't carry much weight. <br /> <br /> And as pointed out by the OP, this is Curseborne, not Scion; mythological accuracy isn't held to the same standard here, rendering it a moot point. If we were discussing a presentation of the Bene Elohim in Scion, that might be a different story; but even there, the Nephilim as giants has about as much grounding in the Bible as Dante's Inferno has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T21:27:19-07:00","id":1564464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561639#post1561639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the same reason we don't see accurate angels: because for most stories it wouldn't be interesting, even if the very few that would, would be quite so.<br /> <br /> You can do a lot more with a humanlike character capable of normal interaction with the others than with an eldritch abomination of an insatiable half-Cthulhu giant.<br /> <br /> Add to that how legends and pop-culture spreads, the fact it wouldn't be intuitive for most people, but mainly because most authors find humanoid characters easier to write about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree on the subject of it not being interesting.<br /> <br /> The idea of taking something that is widely perceived as being holy, and depicting it as something horrifying and destructive can be a far more interesting theme to explore than just a bunch of humans that let divine power go to their heads.<br /> <br /> Kind of gives me Legacy of Kain vibes, where the god that Moebius and the original vampires so devoutly worship turns out to be an eldritch parasite who only regards the souls of its worshipers as a source of food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 10-02-2026, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-02T04:26:42-07:00","id":1564472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1564464#post1564464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I respectfully disagree on the subject of it not being interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because you didn't actually read what I said. Which is something you do often.<br /> <br /> I did not say it wasn't interesting in general. I said it wasn't interesting <i>for most stories</i>.<br /> <br /> Cthulhu is a very interesting entity. But I can't tell a great variety of stories with him. I can tell a few <i>very good ones</i>, but they're few.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T17:44:52-07:00","id":1564769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561642#post1561642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of accurate Nephilim is nonsensical. Accurate to what? The Bible?<br /> <br /> Genesis 6:4 &quot;The Nephilim were in the earth in those days, and also after that, when the Bene Elohim came in unto the daughters of men, and they bore children to them; the same were the mighty men that were of old, the men of renown.&quot;<br /> <br /> I didn't translate Bene Elohim because how you translate it stems from a lot of theological assumptions. But most importantly this is not a phrase that originally meant &quot;angels&quot; as those are divine messengers. The oldest meaning of Bene Elohim would be the deities of the Canaanite pantheon (as the Canaanites treated them as all the sons - Bene - of the high deity El), and pre-hard monotheist Israelite traditions would have also interpreted this similarly. It's only after the Babylonian Exile that Jewish theology shifted towards monotheism and the Israelite deity merged with El, and thus all of the early traditions of the Bene Elohim had to be reconstructed as servants of this new single deity.<br /> <br /> The phrasing itself is unclear if the Nephilim are their own thing, the Bene Elohim that mated with human women, or the offspring who we're supposed to then associate with demigods and mythological heroes from ancient epics (the mighty men and men of renown).<br /> <br /> Numbers 13:33 &quot;And there we saw the Nephilim, the sons of Anak, who come of the Nephilim; and we were in our own sight as grasshoppers, and so we were in their sight.&quot;<br /> <br /> The context of this is that it's the end of the report by the spies sent to scout the land of Canaan before the Israelites end the Exodus and claim the land for themselves. This is where the idea of them being giants probably comes from. Though they're never called giants (and we have characters like Goliath later that repeat the theme of there just being some really big guys among the tribes already living there).<br /> <br /> And that's it. That's all the information you're going to get out of the Bible and older traditions. You have to jump centuries until you get to Enoch 1 and other late post-Exilic writings where we see interpretations of the Nephilim that actually give us any details. And those texts are not uniform in where the Nephilim came from, if they were even inherently bad, and what traits they had that separated them from normal humans.<br /> <br /> Claiming anyone &quot;gets them wrong,&quot; is a far greater negative comment on yourself than it is on any author using them for fiction characters/creatures. If you think there's some authoritative source for an accurate depiction of the Nephilim, you need to do a lot more reading on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as far as I know the word Nephilim did come from the Bible so let's don't be harsh on the guy. He's just looking for accurate Nephilim as far as the Biblical/Historical worldview presented by the Bible goes. Now I'll say this in a RPG the term Nephilim being used for a half angel, half demon, half celestial as I have seen some games do it (Pathfinder 2E for one) is interesting and it leads to paths where much story can be added in but I see no reason why someone could't take these beings offered by the various game systems and &quot;flavor&quot; them however they want. If you want all Nephilim in your game to be more like the Biblical Nephilim that's cool just make a few adjustments, and you have power hungry, gluttonous monsters. That's Pretty much a Story guide's prerogative, however that's probably going to make them less interesting for your player's to play because they are constantly going to be rampaging about and tearing up everything. If that's what the player wants then that's okay but most players want more control over things than that. I am a Christian and I don't really have a problem with taking some creative license with the word Nephilim because Biblically so little is known about them. To learn more that may or may not be true you have to go to the book of Enoch or other extra Biblical sources. It's kind of like Vampire the Masquerade using Cain as the first Vampire utter rubbish as far as reality goes but a nice storyline. One of the things we do when we decide to play RPGs in the first place is decide that we are going to kiss reality goodbye for a little while while we romp around in worlds or multiverses of pure imagination. So if something doesn't mesh with the real world or our view of the real world that's because it's designed not to. It's a feature not necessarily a bug. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1045-zwyt","name":"Zwyt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T18:01:27-07:00","id":1564770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561773#post1561773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DarkKing: You're not asking people to be faithful to real world mythology, you're asking people to be faithful to ancient fanfiction that was rejected by Jewish and early Christian theologians as such.<br /> <br /> Nobody alive today knows how to accurate depict the Nephilim because nobody knows enough about them to do so. Either you have to skip them completely, or treat them as a blank slate just like ancient Exilic Jewish authors did. If you pick the writings of said Exilic writers you're still picking and choosing which you're listening to, and you're inevitably ignoring older source texts on some level.<br /> <br /> As I think I've said enough times, you're talking about <b>my</b> culture's myths. I've written long posts about how wrong people get the Golem myths. I get the desire to have more respectful treatments of real myths, but there's limits. &quot;Nobody knows what accurate would be,&quot; is a limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah most people I think, even Christians and Jews sometime take use a lot of conjecture when it comes to stuff that ancient that only has one or two verses of actual scripture dedicated to it. It's as if God himself didn't count it as that important to the overall theme of the rest of scripture to elaborate more about it. Having said that Enoch who is quoted in the New Testament writes a great deal about the Watchers and the Nephilim but then again we don't know exactly how accurate these writings even from Enoch are. Enoch was a remarkable character in the Bible because he is one of a very few people who it it is said that he walked with God. Then one day he walked with God and he was not for God took him. One of only three assumptions ever recorded in scripture. Enoch, Elijah and Jesus Christ. If you are Jewish you count that as two assumptions I guess Enoch and Elijah. This at any rate is ancient ancient stuff, pre-flood. It's remarkable that we have any record of it at all and we wouldn't if it were not for the sheer tenacity and dedication of Jewish scribes and historians. So if we use a little creative license in coming up with fictional stories about these creatures or beings I don't think it's a huge deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1045-zwyt","name":"Zwyt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T18:19:25-07:00","id":1564771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1564390#post1564390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly reinforcing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> here, but this part was said by spies who were immediately accused of, and punished for, lying about it. So even if you take the Bible seriously, this passage doesn't carry much weight.<br /> <br /> And as pointed out by the OP, this is Curseborne, not Scion; mythological accuracy isn't held to the same standard here, rendering it a moot point. If we were discussing a presentation of the Bene Elohim in Scion, that might be a different story; but even there, the Nephilim as giants has about as much grounding in the Bible as Dante's Inferno has.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the Nephilim are scarcely touched on in scripture and I do take the Bible seriously. But what Dataweaver has said is correct. The information that we are given on Nephilim in actual scripture is scarce, some believe that Goliath was a descendant of the Nephilim, now Goliath was a mean SOB but he wasn't a rampaging monster that was eating everything in sight and destroying everything he touched. In the Bible he is depicted as a Philistine champion who just basically hadn't met anyone who could defeat him so far. Had he been raised away from Philistine society maybe he would have been of a more peaceful demeanor. So even if you go with accurate Nephilim or descendants of the Nephilim as are all of the Accursed they don't have to be like the original Nephilim. I mean none of the Bathorites claim to be Elizabeth Bathory even though we know that's the historical character they are loosely modeled after. So let the extended bloodlines chill them out just a bit. They still have this curse to deal with but none of them are the original article.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1045-zwyt","name":"Zwyt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T23:25:03-07:00","id":1564780,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1045-zwyt\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1045\" data-vbnamecard=\"1045\">Zwyt</a> I think you misunderstood things a little.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> point was precisely what you said. The problem with the OP isn't wanting a particular depiction of the Nephilim, it was judging other choices of depiction because they're &quot;inaccurate&quot;. Heavy was pointing that this notion was actually based on erroneous assumptions, and doing whatever is the actual valid choice because fidelity here is a fool's game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T09:52:57-07:00","id":1565037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561637-why-no-accurate-nephilim?p=1561773#post1561773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DarkKing: You're not asking people to be faithful to real world mythology, you're asking people to be faithful to ancient fanfiction that was rejected by Jewish and early Christian theologians as such.<br /> <br /> Nobody alive today knows how to accurate depict the Nephilim because nobody knows enough about them to do so. Either you have to skip them completely, or treat them as a blank slate just like ancient Exilic Jewish authors did. If you pick the writings of said Exilic writers you're still picking and choosing which you're listening to, and you're inevitably ignoring older source texts on some level.<br /> <br /> As I think I've said enough times, you're talking about <b>my</b> culture's myths. I've written long posts about how wrong people get the Golem myths. I get the desire to have more respectful treatments of real myths, but there's limits. &quot;Nobody knows what accurate would be,&quot; is a limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a Christian and I understand the Nephilims origin as much as IU can given what little information we have but that's not why I like having Nephilim in rpgs. This is a very shallow reason but i like the Nephilim because the freaking name sounds cool! \ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude01\ud83d\ude43","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1045-zwyt","name":"Zwyt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}